# fixedbugs, defect 2034, 2026-10-12, a shape beside the 569 format case.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own whose `printf("%d %d\n", 7)` has
# two conversions and one argument built and printed `7 1807852524` at exit
# 0, then `7 1864541132`, the second number whatever the register held:
# clang's `-Wformat-insufficient-args`, a part of `-Wformat`, went with `-Wall`.
#
# FIX: `-Wformat` stays an error in the region (`emit/header_region.hero`'s
# `KEPT`), and a pragma on a group reaches its parts, so the call is refused
# at the header's line 4.

extern "fixedbugs-2034-a-header-s-own-printf-with-too-few-arguments-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function fmt_shout() -> i32

function main()
    print(fmt_shout())
